        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Linking your Premium X account to Grok after the popup asks you too... might be the most downbad shit I've ever seen from a company.\n\nI suggest none of you do it.\n\nOnce you do it, you lose your X Premium's 20-30 messages per hour to Grok via X, and instead every message is now tied to your weekly usage on Grok.\n\nSo they've essentially clawed back that extra compute you were entitled to via your subscription.\n\nAnd what do you get in return?\n\nNothing... there's 0 benefit to doing this... Linking doesn't even give Grok your X handle context for you to use (like research trends or which posts did well, etc).\n\nIt just steals your usage and spams your grok account with shit (like every time you click grok to get context on a post... that's now a conversation thread). \n\nSpeaking of that... after linking - I Grok'd one post for context. and that shit used 3% of my weekly usage. \n\n3% LMFAO\n\nAnd probs the most insidious part so far - if your SuperGrok subscription is from X Premium (and you previously had gmail+x linked) - unliking that now removes Supergrok. \n\nSo your Grok account becomes free tier lol - meaning you cannot go back to how it was before. Either accept it, or forgo what your subscription originally entitled.\n\nThis is quite possibly the scummiest shit I've ever seen.\n\nLike truly downbad penny pinching between the cushions type shit."
        },
